# Operator Command Lessons Learned

**Activation:** `alwaysApply: false` — when triggers in `agent-discipline-core.mdc` match, **Read this file before editing**. Triggered rules are mandatory, not optional.

Applies when **operator discovery** commands fail, return empty/wrong output, or the same broken paste pattern appears in multiple plans.

## Law (non-negotiable)

When an operator reports that a **Pending commands** block failed (wrong path, wrong user, missing overlay file, grep too broad, empty result, permission denied, etc.):

1. **Fix the plan in the same turn** — update **Operator discovery** on disk (`plan-live-disk-sync.mdc`); record what failed in **Completed findings**.
2. **Update `compose-operator-terminal-commands.mdc` in the same task** — add or extend:
   - **Anti-pattern** — what failed and why (one line).
   - **Corrected pattern** — copy/paste block that works on this deployment shape.
   - Optional **Lessons learned** bullet under the relevant section (logs, INI paths, service choice).
3. **Do not reuse** the failed command verbatim in future plans — cite the corrected rule text instead.

If the failure reveals a **recurring** gap (not a one-off typo), also add a one-line cross-link in **`deploy-ini-with-code-no-phase-zero.mdc`** or **`hpcperfstats-ini-format.mdc`** when INI/path semantics were wrong.

## What counts as “failed”

- Non-zero exit, `command not found`, wrong container user (`su hpcperfstats` vs root).
- Path does not exist — especially when the command hardcoded `/hpcperfstats/...` instead of INI-resolved paths.
- Leading `cd HPCPerfStats` (or any host `cd`) before `docker compose` in operator paste blocks — forbidden per **Mandatory format** in `compose-operator-terminal-commands.mdc`; state cwd in prose only.
- `docker compose logs pipeline --tail=N` (with or without grep) on long-running pipeline — truncates before stall window; see **No `--tail` on `compose logs`** in `compose-operator-terminal-commands.mdc`.
- Nested multi-layer `sh -lc` + `python3 -c` quoting through podman-compose — **`unexpected EOF while looking for matching '"'`** (hpcperfstats03 2026-07-22); use a single `su hpcperfstats -c 'python3 -c "…"'` (see **Podman-compose sites** nested-quoting row in `compose-operator-terminal-commands.mdc`).
- Nested `sh -lc` around a deploy-fingerprint `python3 -c` (die-zombies / Branch R) — same EOF on hpcperfstats01 2026-07-25; **split** Python fingerprint and shell PID census into two `podman exec` blocks (see **Podman-compose sites** fingerprint row).
- Treating RC-JT terminate/reap **source fingerprint True** as proof idle hygiene runs — overnight dual-site 2026-07-26 (Branch Z-H2) had fingerprint True + hygiene **count 0** + multi-hour zombies; always count full-buffer hygiene signatures (see **Podman-compose sites** hygiene rows).
- `grep | tail && next_cmd` for hygiene/exit forensics — empty grep exits 1 and **short-circuits** the census; use `grep -cE … || true` and separate blocks (see **Podman-compose sites** `grep|tail &&` row).
- `docker compose exec pipeline python3 - <<'PY'` (heredoc through exec) on podman-compose — opens interactive REPL instead of running script; use `su hpcperfstats -c 'python3 -c "…"'` per **Podman-compose sites** anti-patterns in `compose-operator-terminal-commands.mdc`.
- `find … | wc -l` under nested quoting / `/usr/bin/time` missing in pipeline — false-zero counts; use bash `TIMEFORMAT` + `find … -printf '.' | wc -c` (see **Podman-compose sites** find rows in `compose-operator-terminal-commands.mdc`).
- Bare `python3 -c` importing `sync_timedb_ingest_readiness` / `host_data` without **`ensure_django()`** — `ImproperlyConfigured` (hpcperfstats03); see **Django bootstrap** anti-pattern in `compose-operator-terminal-commands.mdc`. Same signature for **`scripts/migrate_daily_archive_gz_to_zst.py`** when the image predates the script/`build_archive_maintenance_snapshot` bootstrap fix — redeploy before re-running migrate.
- Inventing `calendar_date_from_stats_path` — **ImportError** on hpcperfstats03; use `daily_tar_path_for_stats_path` + `calendar_date_from_daily_tar_path` (see **Anti-pattern — inventing `calendar_date_from_stats_path`** in `compose-operator-terminal-commands.mdc`).
- Inventing `{archive}/.sync_timedb_unparsable_raw/manifest.json` — **`manifest_exists False`** while quarantine moves still run; real sidecar is **`{archive}/.sync_timedb_unparsable_raw.json`** via **`manifest_path_for_archive`** (see **Anti-pattern — inventing unparsable-raw `manifest.json`** in `compose-operator-terminal-commands.mdc`).
- Wrong Redis key names for archive populate degraded / day skip — bare `*populate_degraded*` / `…:populate_degraded:v1:` returns empty while real keys are **`archive_populate_degraded`** / **`archive_day_ingest_skip`** (see **Anti-pattern — wrong archive_populate Redis key names** in `compose-operator-terminal-commands.mdc`).
- Hardcoded `/hpcperfstats/…` or raw ConfigParser for `archive_dir` in Pending blocks — preToolUse deny (`check-live-plan-operator-discovery.py`).
- Introspection misuse — unbounded `strace`, `gdb` left attached, or `py-spy` without a target PID when `pgrep`/`ps` should run first (see **Container introspection tools** in `compose-operator-terminal-commands.mdc`).
- Missing `-f docker-compose.app.yaml` (or other overlay) when production uses it.
- Duplicate command blocks that already failed in an earlier plan for the same site.
- Treat `ls *.fnctl.lock` / sidecar presence as a held lock — orphans are common; `fuser` often missing in pipeline image; use `try_file_write_lock` (see **Podman-compose sites** `fnctl.lock` row in `compose-operator-terminal-commands.mdc`).
- `docker compose … up -d web` after a crash-loop on **podman-compose** — **name already in use** / exit **125**; use `podman start hpcperfstats_web_1` or `podman rm -f` then up (see **Podman-compose sites** in `compose-operator-terminal-commands.mdc`).
- Treating `job_data.host_list` as a CSV `text` — **`btrim(text[]) does not exist`** (hpcperfstats03 2026-07-23); column is **`text[]`** — use `hd.host = ANY (j.host_list)` / `unnest(host_list)` (see **Anti-pattern — `job_data.host_list` is `text[]`** in `compose-operator-terminal-commands.mdc`).
- Broad `host_data` wall-clock scans with **`ILIKE '%…%'`** / multi-host **`ANY(host_list)`** / **`OR hd.jid`** — **`canceling statement due to statement timeout`** (hpcperfstats03 2026-07-23); use **one host** (`host_list[1]`), exact `type`/`event` lists, and `SET statement_timeout` (see **Corrected — host_data …** in `compose-operator-terminal-commands.mdc`).
- One-host exact-event **`GROUP BY` over full accounting `start`/`end`** still timed out at **120s** on a long job (hpcperfstats03 2026-07-23 JID 857260); use **telemetry time bounds** + **single event** + **`ORDER BY time DESC LIMIT N`**, or rely on **`metrics_data`** when already poisoned (see **Corrected — host_data poison / event probe** in `compose-operator-terminal-commands.mdc`).
- Even **telemetry+LIMIT 20** one-host probes can **still timeout at 60s** (hpcperfstats03 2026-07-23 finding #7); when poison is already in **`metrics_data`**, skip raw `host_data` entirely (see **Anti-pattern — assume telemetry+LIMIT always finishes**).
- Empty host+telemetry GPU probes while **`metrics_data` shows GPU poison** (hpcperfstats01 JID `3351747`, 2026-07-31) are **not** “no GPU telemetry” — ground on `metrics_data` (see **Anti-pattern — empty host+telemetry GPU probe** in `compose-operator-terminal-commands.mdc`).
- No-artifact prevalence cohorts without **`metrics_distinct_time_count__gte=N`** measure incomplete-metrics noise, not 857260-class gaps (see **Anti-pattern — no-artifact cohorts without metrics readiness**).
- Nested multi-line `manage.py shell -c` pastes can **mangle trailing queries** on podman-compose (hpcperfstats03 2026-07-23); prefer short scripts / fewer nested escapes (see **Anti-pattern — fragile nested `manage.py shell -c` pastes**).
- Inventing `job_data.metrics_complete` — **`FieldError`**; use **`metrics_distinct_time_count`** (see **Anti-pattern — inventing `job_data.metrics_complete`** in `compose-operator-terminal-commands.mdc`).
- Inventing `job_detail_artifact.schema_version` / `fingerprint` — **`FieldError`**; use **`artifact_schema`** / **`input_fingerprint`** (see **Anti-pattern — inventing `job_detail_artifact.schema_version` / `fingerprint`** in `compose-operator-terminal-commands.mdc`).
- `host_data.filter(jid=…, type=\"nvidia_gpu\", event__in=[power/util/count])` returning **empty** while Job Detail shows GPU poison — host stats often lack accounting `jid`; use `job_data` → `metrics_data` by jid, then `host`+telemetry window (hpcperfstats01 JID `3351747`, 2026-07-30; see **Anti-pattern — `host_data.filter(jid=…)` for GPU** in `compose-operator-terminal-commands.mdc`).

## Same-task checklist

| Step | Action |
|------|--------|
| 1 | Operator paste or error message captured in plan **Completed findings** |
| 2 | Pending block removed or replaced with corrected block |
| 3 | **`compose-operator-terminal-commands.mdc`** updated (anti-pattern + fix) |
| 4 | New plans use the corrected pattern only |

## Narrow exceptions

- One-off operator typo in the paste (operator ran the wrong block) — fix the plan only; no rule edit required.
- Environment outage (compose down, disk full) — document blocker in plan; no rule change unless the command shape was wrong.

## Overlap

- **`compose-operator-terminal-commands.mdc`** — authoritative command shape; this rule requires **writing back** failures into that file.
- **`plan-live-disk-sync.mdc`** — findings and pending updates on disk only.
- **`deploy-ini-with-code-no-phase-zero.mdc`** — read-only gathering; failures often mean paths should have come from INI first.
- **`hpcperfstats-ini-format.mdc`** — INI key names and sections for path resolution.
